{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>It is good.</b> I have already explained in the verse 'anger is better than laughter' — it concerns the portions of the soul. The man of understanding gives each portion of the soul its due in its time, and has no need to seek what to do; rather he follows the Torah of our Elohim and does not turn from it right or left, and keeps the commandments, 'which a person shall do and live by them' — in both worlds. And on this matter he sealed his book: 'one who fears Elohim will come forth from all of them' — in truth."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:12.332140291Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}